`ExperimentConfig(sample_weight="group")` weights each training fold so that each group (e.g. a subject) counts once within each class, with `coco_pipe.utils.balanced_sample_weights`, which dimensionality-reduction evaluation also uses. `FoundationClassifier.fit` takes `sample_weight`, which weights each window's loss. Decoding fits now pass sample weights, groups and conditions through scikit-learn's metadata routing, so sample weights, these or `Experiment.run(sample_weight=...)`, reach every pipeline step whose `fit` takes them (the scaler included), the inner fits and scorers of tuning and sequential feature selection, the calibrator, and each permutation of a permutation test; a classifier that cannot take them is refused instead of skipped.
